/**
\mainpage Qore PDF Module

\section pdfintro pdf Module Introduction

    <img src="pdf-logo.svg" width="96" alt="pdf module logo"/>

    The <tt>pdf</tt> module provides PDF functionality for Qore using QPDF and PoDoFo,
with optional PDFium support for rendering and text extraction.

    @section pdfqlibmodules Qore User Modules

    - @ref pdfdataproviderintro "PdfDataProvider" — a data provider API for PDF documents

\section pdffeatures Features

- Create PDFs with PoDoFo
- Read/edit/merge/split PDFs with QPDF
- Optional rendering and text extraction with PDFium
- Data provider actions for Qorus integration via @ref pdfdataproviderintro "PdfDataProvider"

\section pdfdataprovider PdfDataProvider Module

The @ref pdfdataproviderintro "PdfDataProvider" module provides integration with Qore's
DataProvider API. See the @ref pdfdataproviderintro "PdfDataProvider module documentation"
for complete API reference.

\section pdfdataprov Data Provider Actions

The module ships with PdfDataProvider for Qore's data provider framework.
Example <tt>qdp</tt> commands:

\code{.bash}
qdp 'pdf{}/document/create' output_path=out.pdf,page_count=2
qdp 'pdf{}/document/info' input_path=out.pdf
qdp 'pdf{}/document/metadata' input_path=out.pdf,output_path=meta.pdf,metadata='{"title":"Updated"}'
qdp 'pdf{}/document/merge' inputs='("a.pdf","b.pdf")',output_path=merged.pdf
qdp 'pdf{}/document/rotate' input_path=out.pdf,output_path=rotated.pdf,pages='(0)',degrees=90
qdp 'pdf{}/render/page' input_path=out.pdf,page_index=0,dpi=150
qdp 'pdf{}/render/extract-text' input_path=out.pdf,page_index=0
\endcode

\section pdfcallerpaths Paths and Restricted Code

The methods that take a file path, and the \c font_path of a font given to
@ref Qore::Pdf::PdfEditor::drawText() "PdfEditor::drawText()", refuse the path with \c PERMISSION-DENIED before
anything is read or written if the code that gives it is restricted from the \c FILESYSTEM functional domain (for
example with \c PO_NO_FILESYSTEM).  The methods with the \c FILESYSTEM functional domain cannot be called by such
code at all; a method of an object of a module class that the host created and gave to restricted code, however,
runs with the file system lent, so the paths that such a method gives these classes are decided with the code that
the object was given to (with a %Qore that provides \c qore_caller_lent_to_restricts_domain(), which defines
\c QORE_HAVE_CALLER_AMBIENT_PREDICATES; built with an older %Qore, only the calling code decides, and only for a
\c font_path; @ref Qore::Pdf::PDF_LENT_PATH_CHECKS tells which).  The file-system policy of a sandbox that governs the calling code applies when a file is opened
(\c FILESYSTEM-ACCESS-DENIED).  Documents, images and fonts given as data, and the state of an existing object (its
document, its font options), can be used by restricted code.

\section pdfdependencies Dependencies

- QPDF (required)
- PoDoFo (required; bundled by default, LGPL-2.0-or-later)
- PDFium (optional)

\section pdfpackages OS Packages

The bundled PoDoFo build requires common graphics/font libraries. PDFium is
optional; there is no MacPorts PDFium port.

\subsection packages_ubuntu Ubuntu

\code{.bash}
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y \
  cmake pkg-config qpdf libqpdf-dev libfreetype-dev \
  libssl-dev libxml2-dev libfontconfig1-dev libpng-dev \
  libjpeg-turbo8-dev libtiff-dev zlib1g-dev
\endcode

PDFium (optional): not packaged in standard Ubuntu repos; provide a prebuilt
<tt>libpdfium</tt> and pass <tt>-DENABLE_PDFIUM=ON -DPDFIUM_INCLUDE_DIR=... -DPDFIUM_LIBRARY=...</tt>,
or use <tt>-DENABLE_PDFIUM=OFF</tt>.

\subsection packages_alpine Alpine

\code{.bash}
sudo apk add --no-cache \
  cmake pkgconfig qpdf qpdf-dev freetype-dev \
  openssl-dev libxml2-dev fontconfig-dev libpng-dev \
  libjpeg-turbo-dev tiff-dev zlib-dev
\endcode

PDFium (optional): not in Alpine repos; provide a prebuilt <tt>libpdfium</tt> and pass
<tt>-DENABLE_PDFIUM=ON -DPDFIUM_INCLUDE_DIR=... -DPDFIUM_LIBRARY=...</tt>,
or use <tt>-DENABLE_PDFIUM=OFF</tt>.

\subsection packages_fedora Fedora

\code{.bash}
sudo dnf install -y \
  cmake pkgconf-pkg-config qpdf qpdf-devel freetype-devel \
  openssl-devel libxml2-devel fontconfig-devel libpng-devel \
  libjpeg-turbo-devel libtiff-devel zlib-devel
\endcode

\subsection packages_macports MacPorts

\code{.bash}
sudo port install \
  cmake pkgconfig qpdf freetype openssl3 libxml2 fontconfig libpng \
  libjpeg-turbo tiff zlib
\endcode

